@startuml
'=============================================================================
' KIND      MEASURED -- every state below is a literal written into the
'           worker's ledger by fleet/inbox.py, and every terminal state is
'           a member of that module's TERMINAL tuple.
' GROUNDING fleet/inbox.py: poll(), _poll_contract_item(), reconcile(),
'           item_state(), TERMINAL, IDENTITY_POLICIES, FOLDERS.
'
' This is the RUNTIME work item -- one arriving file. It is a different
' object from the DEVELOPMENT work item in 04-development-workflow.puml,
' and the two state machines must not be read as one.
'=============================================================================
!theme plain
title Learning Lab — runtime work-item states (MEASURED)

[*] --> Waiting : file arrives in inbox/

state Waiting
state Claimed
state Staged
state Completed
state Exception
state SkippedDuplicate as "skipped_duplicate"
state RecoveredCompleted as "recovered_completed"
state RecoveredException as "recovered_exception"

Waiting --> Exception : unreadable item\n(moved to exceptions/)
Waiting --> SkippedDuplicate : already completed under this\ncontent digest -- NOT re-run,\nand its effect NOT re-applied
Waiting --> Staged : contract path: the input set\nis still partial
Waiting --> Claimed : claimed BEFORE the run,\nwith a recorded precondition

Staged --> Staged : re-poll skips it; the SET,\nnot the file location, is\nthe authority
Staged --> Claimed : the last required slot arrives

Claimed --> Completed : healthy
Claimed --> Exception : refused or failed\n(moved to exceptions/)

Claimed --> RecoveredCompleted : recovery: already_landed,\nor safe_to_retry then healthy
Claimed --> RecoveredException : recovery: indeterminate,\nor retried and unhealthy

Completed --> [*]
Exception --> [*]
SkippedDuplicate --> [*]
RecoveredCompleted --> [*]
RecoveredException --> [*]

note right of Claimed
The claim is written **before** the effect,
with the precondition it observed. An
interrupted pass therefore leaves evidence
rather than a fresh-looking file.
end note

note as N1
**Recovery verdicts** (fleet/inbox.py reconcile)

  already_landed   effect absent at claim time, present now
                   -> complete WITHOUT re-executing
  safe_to_retry    definitely absent, or none was earnable
                   -> re-execute
  indeterminate    the question cannot be answered
                   -> exception, never guessed either way

"Definitely absent" and "cannot tell" lead to opposite actions.
Collapsing them would retry a booking that may already exist,
which is why `effect_landed` returns None rather than False when
worker state is unreadable.
end note

note as N2
**Item identity**

`work_item_identity` has exactly one implemented policy,
`content_digest`. A worker that declares nothing, or something
else, is REFUSED -- the policy is not defaulted.

That identity is what makes `skipped_duplicate` safe: the same
bytes arriving twice is the same work item, not new work.
end note
@enduml
